1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:11,969
Meet Cowork Value Intelligence: one Power BI report that turns Cowork activity into a clear story about adoption, the work people delegate, how deeply they delegate it, and the value those workflows may create.

2
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:17,120
The template is data-free by design and comes to life with your approved organization exports.

3
00:00:17,121 --> 00:00:20,223
Here is a quick tour of the decisions it supports.

4
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:23,262
Start Here is home base.

5
00:00:23,263 --> 00:00:27,130
It routes leaders to the questions that matter: Is adoption growing?

6
00:00:27,131 --> 00:00:29,071
Who is using Cowork?

7
00:00:29,072 --> 00:00:31,248
What work is being delegated?

8
00:00:31,249 --> 00:00:33,413
Where is value concentrating?

9
00:00:33,414 --> 00:00:35,723
Which workflows need enablement?

10
00:00:35,724 --> 00:00:37,598
What should happen next?

11
00:00:37,599 --> 00:00:41,505
The report begins with the decision and guides you to the right evidence.

12
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:52,698
Activity and Value shows where Cowork is becoming part of everyday work: which skills are used most, which categories contribute the most estimated hours, and which departments are building momentum.

13
00:00:52,699 --> 00:00:56,499
This turns generic training into targeted workflow enablement.

14
00:00:57,256 --> 00:01:00,453
Actions explains what people ask Cowork to do.

15
00:01:00,454 --> 00:01:08,071
Move from skill volume to work categories and value tiers, spot unmapped tools, and identify repeatable actions worth scaling.

16
00:01:08,072 --> 00:01:10,414
The goal is not more prompts.

17
00:01:10,415 --> 00:01:12,970
It is better, higher-value work.

18
00:01:13,723 --> 00:01:16,786
How Far They Delegate goes beyond activity.

19
00:01:16,787 --> 00:01:23,756
It shows task duration, steps, skill chaining, and movement from trying to using, delegating, and automating.

20
00:01:23,757 --> 00:01:29,962
These signals show workflow depth—not unattended work—and where users are ready for advanced patterns.

21
00:01:30,723 --> 00:01:35,159
Value by User Tier reveals whether adoption is broad or concentrated.

22
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:41,582
Find champions who can teach proven patterns, teams that depend on a few experts, and users who may need coaching.

23
00:01:41,583 --> 00:01:44,998
Pair each tier with business context before acting.

24
00:01:45,756 --> 00:01:49,344
The methodology page keeps the value story defensible.

25
00:01:49,345 --> 00:01:57,341
Every output traces to observed task volume, published time-saved assumptions, a selected labor rate, and optional quality adjustments.

26
00:01:57,342 --> 00:02:00,354
Change the assumptions and the result changes.

27
00:02:00,355 --> 00:02:03,847
This is scenario planning, not audited savings.

28
00:02:04,596 --> 00:02:09,356
Together, these views answer the questions leaders have: Is adoption growing?

29
00:02:09,357 --> 00:02:11,482
What work is being delegated?

30
00:02:11,483 --> 00:02:14,172
Are people moving into deeper workflows?

31
00:02:14,173 --> 00:02:15,946
Where are the champions?

32
00:02:15,947 --> 00:02:18,379
Which patterns should we scale next?

33
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:23,804
Consumption and cost are available when needed, but they support the story—they do not define it.

34
00:02:24,564 --> 00:02:30,853
That is Cowork Value Intelligence: one report from activity to a defensible value and enablement story.

35
00:02:30,854 --> 00:02:37,934
Download the template, connect your approved exports, and turn your organization's Cowork activity into an actionable value story.

